Root Cause Analysis:
The error is due to the `generateTag` function in the TypeScript codebase producing a string with the prefix "DOG-" instead of the expected "CATA-". This discrepancy is causing the unit test to fail, as it expects the generated tag to start with "CATA-".

File to Fix:
`src/utils/tagGenerator.ts`

Fixed Code:
```typescript
// src/utils/tagGenerator.ts

function generateTag(): string {
    // The function was incorrectly generating tags with "DOG-" prefix
    // Changed the prefix to "CATA-" to match the expected pattern in tests
    const prefix = "CATA-";
    const uniqueId = Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9).toUpperCase();
    return `${prefix}${uniqueId}`;
}

export default generateTag;
```

